  "purpose": "QR-QBANK 13b (10-21 17:30): structural successor of qbank12a (gate ot-epyc9 FAIL clock_rule only: ONE TritonCTS tree from ck over 950x475 um, 13,775 sinks (12k pin/stage flops + the 1,664 QB_WLOCAL macro-local write-port flops beside the 8 SRAMs), TT insertion 802 / pin-flop spread 166.9 ps, FF 657 / 145.6 ps; trial GRT overflow 0) and of qbank11a (route TT -483.8: reg->macro write pins, one p_dd bit -> 17 wd pins over the 160-um face; fixed by the kept 2-hop QB_WLOCAL write-port copies, kept here, <=32 loads/driver). Fix (regional clock, FALLBACK): TritonCTS kept but with per-region register clustering: <=16 sinks within 25 um per leaf (was 30/40), 3 clustering levels (region -> macro column -> root, was 2), repeater every 40 um on the H-tree trunks (no long strung leaf nets to the macro-face copies). Same RTL/geometry as 12a (0 cycles).",
